abstract: >
  A configuration-driven Python pipeline for assessing solar resource
  potential (Global Horizontal Irradiance) across multiple countries.
  Includes a quality-assurance module (CRS/pixel plausibility, physical
  plausibility, boundary/raster area consistency, administrative
  topology, threshold plausibility), raster-based zonal statistics for
  scalable per-admin-unit analysis, and automated per-country and
  cross-country HTML/JSON reporting. Generalizes the single-country
  methodology developed for reunion-solar-analysis
  (https://github.com/lenzchery/reunion-solar-analysis) to six countries
  spanning a wide range of raster sizes, administrative unit counts, and
  coordinate reference systems.

